# Web Cabinet

- This is an operator/study cockpit, not a public SaaS landing page. Keep the interface quiet, dense, readable, and work-focused.
- Preserve authenticated owner/admin flows and avoid exposing private Telegram IDs, raw clinical records, provider tokens, or generated audit artifacts.
- Prefer readable sections for weak topics, due cards, feedback, high-risk counts, search misses, source coverage, AI routing, and go/no-go health over raw JSON dumps.
- Keep UI states complete: loading, empty, error, unauthorized, and successful update states.
- Follow the existing React/Vite style before adding new UI libraries. Avoid broad restyles unless the task is explicitly a redesign.
- Text must fit in compact cards, tables, sidebars, and buttons on mobile and desktop.

## Useful Checks

```powershell
cd web
npm test
npm run build
npm audit --omit=dev
```
